In SvelteKit, `+server.ts` files export named handlers for each HTTP method: `GET`, `POST`, `PUT`, `DELETE`, `PATCH`, `OPTIONS`, `HEAD`. If a method isn't exported, SvelteKit returns a 405 Method Not Allowed (or falls through to other route matches).

The scraper endpoint only exports `GET`. So only GET requests are handled. There's no fallback that could bypass auth.

