```typescript
export function validateDebugToken(authHeader: string | null, expectedToken: string | undefined): boolean {
  if (!expectedToken || !authHeader) return false;
  return authHeader === `Bearer ${expectedToken}`;
}
```

If `expectedToken` is `undefined`, `!expectedToken` is `true`, returns `false`. Good.
If `expectedToken` is `''` (empty string), `!expectedToken` is `true`, returns `false`. Good.
If `authHeader` is `null`, `!authHeader` is `true`, returns `false`. Good.

This is robust.

